1
00:00:49,050 --> 00:00:52,990
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:56,020
[Episode 5]

3
00:00:56,610 --> 00:00:57,700
I've got a way

4
00:00:58,210 --> 00:01:00,170
to let you see what he looks like.

5
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:02,420
What,

6
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:04,980
you can get the Yellow Immortal

7
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:06,230
to take a picture of him?

8
00:01:06,870 --> 00:01:08,010
Do you want to see?

9
00:01:08,010 --> 00:01:09,289
Just spit it out.

10
00:01:13,430 --> 00:01:15,120
Hello, Officer Liu.

11
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:18,750
Um,

12
00:01:20,610 --> 00:01:21,280
um,

13
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:22,940
O-Officer Liu is right here.

14
00:01:25,150 --> 00:01:25,840
Okay.

15
00:01:26,610 --> 00:01:28,550
Hello, Officer Liu.

16
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:29,800
Hello, Mr. Wu.

17
00:01:29,830 --> 00:01:30,700
Oh, no need to be so formal.

18
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:31,920
Just call me Liu Juan.

19
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:35,509
Mr. Wu is an art teacher
at No. 4 Middle School.

20
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:38,350
He also takes on side jobs,

21
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:39,870
painting portraits of the deceased
for their families.

22
00:01:40,289 --> 00:01:41,880
He's incredibly skilled.

23
00:01:42,430 --> 00:01:43,630
He doesn't even need a photo.

24
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:45,560
Just from the family's description,

25
00:01:45,590 --> 00:01:46,930
he can paint a deceased elderly person

26
00:01:46,930 --> 00:01:49,150
so true to life.

27
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:49,840
You're too kind.

28
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:51,180
-You're too modest. You really are.
-You are...

29
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:51,840
Mr. Wu,

30
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:53,060
if you don't mind me asking...

31
00:01:53,060 --> 00:01:54,640
Would you say you only paint the elderly,

32
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:56,789
or can you paint people
of all ages and both genders?

33
00:01:59,070 --> 00:01:59,979
I can paint anyone.

34
00:02:00,340 --> 00:02:01,010
Great.

35
00:02:01,010 --> 00:02:01,930
Then let's get started.

36
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:03,330
Yes, let's start painting.

37
00:02:03,350 --> 00:02:03,850
So...

38
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:05,710
Officer Liu,

39
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:09,300
am I painting someone who's dead or alive?

40
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:15,660
Please describe
this person's appearance to me,

41
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:18,790
in as much detail as possible.

42
00:02:21,090 --> 00:02:22,950
T-This person

43
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:24,300
is in his twenties.

44
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:26,930
In his twenties.

45
00:02:26,930 --> 00:02:28,780
Yeah, h-he's in his twenties.

46
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:29,540
In his twenties.

47
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:31,840
His face...

48
00:02:32,410 --> 00:02:34,190
Is it long... or not?

49
00:02:34,590 --> 00:02:35,079
It's long

50
00:02:35,079 --> 00:02:35,470
Long.

51
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:36,130
A long, thin face.

52
00:02:36,130 --> 00:02:36,520
Long and thin.

53
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,530
-A long, thin face, yeah.
-Long and thin.

54
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:38,030
A long, thin face.

55
00:02:38,030 --> 00:02:40,110
When it comes to painting,

56
00:02:40,140 --> 00:02:42,880
you should at least be able
to see what you're painting, right?

57
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:44,410
You... This...

58
00:02:45,150 --> 00:02:47,300
If you can't even see...
Mr. Wu...

59
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:49,520
Look, his eyesight isn't good at all.

60
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:50,150
There are.

61
00:02:50,150 --> 00:02:51,430
-Well, you never know.
-There are plenty.

62
00:02:51,430 --> 00:02:51,930
Plenty?

63
00:02:51,930 --> 00:02:52,520
Yeah, plenty.

64
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:53,870
Beethoven, who played piano,

65
00:02:53,870 --> 00:02:55,030
was deaf.

66
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,120
Right?

67
00:02:56,930 --> 00:02:58,120
That's true.

68
00:02:58,470 --> 00:02:59,300
What about his hair?

69
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,150
His hair...

70
00:03:01,930 --> 00:03:03,500
It's long and really messy.

71
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:04,300
Messy.

72
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:05,250
-Really messy.
-Messy works. Messy works for me.

73
00:03:05,250 --> 00:03:07,190
-Messy works. Messy works for me.
-People always say

74
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:08,690
that artists

75
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:10,520
work their minds.

76
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:13,520
He's devoted,
and it shows from the inside out.

77
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,250
And

78
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:17,340
I bought Mr. Wu a bottle of liquor

79
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:18,530
and a carton of cigarettes. 48 in total.

80
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:19,410
Don't forget to pay me back.

81
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:23,000
You're really something.

82
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:28,870
Ten, twenty,

83
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:30,560
thirty, forty, fifty.

84
00:03:30,590 --> 00:03:32,030
Fine, fine. Just give me fifty.

85
00:03:32,430 --> 00:03:33,600
Give me two back.

86
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:35,860
Why are you asking for change?

87
00:03:36,870 --> 00:03:38,020
Didn't I go through all that trouble
to buy them? I—

88
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:39,030
Come on, quit talking

89
00:03:39,030 --> 00:03:39,780
and give me two bucks.

90
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,430
Here, here.

91
00:03:48,690 --> 00:03:49,500
Does this look like him?

92
00:03:52,090 --> 00:03:52,740
Yeah.

93
00:03:53,130 --> 00:03:53,910
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

94
00:03:53,910 --> 00:03:54,680
Yeah, yeah.

95
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,520
That's him. No doubt about it. That's him.

96
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:56,970
It's him?

97
00:03:56,970 --> 00:03:57,430
That's him.

98
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:04,560
Mr. Wu,

99
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:06,650
you're

100
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:08,310
an abstract artist, aren't you?

101
00:04:16,829 --> 00:04:20,100
[Limin Bookstore] [Cashier]

102
00:04:57,070 --> 00:04:58,360
Do you want to buy a book?

103
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:22,790
[Limin Bookstore] [Cashier]

104
00:05:53,010 --> 00:05:54,640
Hi. Can you ring this up for me?

105
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:55,360
Sure.

106
00:05:55,450 --> 00:05:56,120
Eighteen.

107
00:05:56,830 --> 00:05:57,300
Here.

108
00:05:58,740 --> 00:05:59,480
This one looks good.

109
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:03,740
Come on, let's go.

110
00:06:04,190 --> 00:06:04,810
Let's go.

111
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:55,540
Thanks.

112
00:06:58,250 --> 00:06:58,920
Does it hurt?

113
00:07:04,630 --> 00:07:05,630
This is nothing.

114
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:16,510
What kind of book are you reading?

115
00:07:18,770 --> 00:07:20,130
"Jonathan Livingston Seagull."

116
00:07:20,130 --> 00:07:21,000
Seagulls?

117
00:07:21,310 --> 00:07:22,310
If you want to watch seagulls,

118
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:24,450
just watch "Animal World."

119
00:07:24,930 --> 00:07:26,040
Why tire yourself out
reading all those words?

120
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:40,690
What's it about?

121
00:07:40,690 --> 00:07:42,250
Is it about seagulls, or...

122
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:45,159
It's a story about learning to fly.

123
00:07:45,810 --> 00:07:46,770
It's a metaphor.

124
00:07:51,450 --> 00:07:52,750
I don't like reading this kind of thing.

125
00:07:54,750 --> 00:07:56,680
I always feel like
they've got something to say

126
00:07:57,980 --> 00:07:59,420
but won't say it straight—

127
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:00,450
they just make things up.

128
00:08:05,330 --> 00:08:06,600
Isn't that

129
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,390
what life is all about?

130
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:10,620
Do it well,

131
00:08:11,130 --> 00:08:12,220
and life treats you well.

132
00:08:12,630 --> 00:08:13,920
Do it badly,

133
00:08:14,570 --> 00:08:15,630
and you just have to tough it out.

134
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:17,480
Just like me.

135
00:08:26,390 --> 00:08:27,680
You haven't been back in a long time.

136
00:08:29,130 --> 00:08:30,620
There's a lot you don't know.

137
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:34,630
Have you got a girlfriend?

138
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:37,820
Yeah.

139
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:42,580
Several, actually.

140
00:08:44,030 --> 00:08:45,200
At the

141
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,700
Workers' School,

142
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:49,120
I had girlfriends

143
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,220
in both girls' dorms.

144
00:08:51,510 --> 00:08:52,550
Later,

145
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:54,960
I got another one at my workplace.

146
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:56,770
I didn't like her stained teeth,

147
00:08:56,770 --> 00:08:57,740
so I didn't bother with her.

148
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:28,250
Look at how dry your lips are.

149
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:29,980
They're all peeling.

150
00:09:43,910 --> 00:09:45,220
After work,

151
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:46,830
come with me somewhere.

152
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:48,830
[Emergency]

153
00:09:48,850 --> 00:09:51,580
[Dialysis Room]

154
00:09:58,470 --> 00:10:07,790
[Blood Purification Center]

155
00:10:12,050 --> 00:10:14,270
Are all the people here on dialysis?

156
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:16,910
Yes, twice a week.

157
00:10:16,930 --> 00:10:18,460
The schedule is fixed.

158
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:21,410
How do people end up with uremia?

159
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:24,070
All sorts of ways.

160
00:10:24,670 --> 00:10:26,300
Some get it from diabetes.

161
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:27,740
Some get it from a poor diet

162
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:28,910
and unhealthy drinking habits.

163
00:10:30,270 --> 00:10:31,170
Put simply,

164
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:32,980
some people are just unlucky.

165
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:34,910
Come on, let me check your fistula.

166
00:10:43,610 --> 00:10:45,040
Looks good. Go on in.

167
00:10:56,650 --> 00:10:59,530
C-Can this disease be cured?

168
00:10:56,650 --> 00:10:57,100
This...

169
00:11:01,290 --> 00:11:02,390
The doctor said

170
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:03,990
dialysis alone

171
00:11:04,030 --> 00:11:05,440
will only keep you going
for another ten years or so.

172
00:11:05,670 --> 00:11:07,270
If you want to get back to normal,

173
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:09,510
you'd need a kidney transplant.

174
00:11:53,440 --> 00:11:55,600
Are you here with a family member?

175
00:12:01,410 --> 00:12:02,170
My partner.

176
00:12:09,090 --> 00:12:18,160
[Dialysis Room]

177
00:12:28,390 --> 00:12:29,290
Scared you, huh?

178
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,480
It is what it is.

179
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:42,650
Everyone who comes here
does so to stay alive.

180
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:54,220
That's right.

181
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:56,200
I understand.

182
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:01,480
When it comes to staying alive,

183
00:13:04,510 --> 00:13:05,890
nothing is too much.

184
00:15:58,630 --> 00:15:59,790
He got what he deserved.

185
00:15:59,810 --> 00:16:01,760
This fire is Heaven's will.

186
00:16:02,300 --> 00:16:04,160
If there's a debt to be paid,
let the debtor pay it.

187
00:16:04,190 --> 00:16:05,670
I'm sorry, man.

188
00:16:07,310 --> 00:16:09,370
I know exactly

189
00:16:09,690 --> 00:16:11,380
how the three of them died.
